.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-TIMESTAMP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-timestamp
.Nd add an RFC 3161 timestamp to a sealed capsule
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis timestamp
.Fl -tsa Ar url ...
.Op Fl -anchor Ar der-file ...
.Op Fl -force
.Ar dir
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis timestamp
asks a time-stamping authority (RFC 3161) for a token over the signature
of the capsule
.Ar dir ,
sealed before with
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 ,
and stores it in
.Pa noqtis.sig .
The manifest
.Pa noqtis.json
and the signature are not changed, so the capsule still checks; with the
TSA's certificate as an anchor,
.Xr noqtis-check 1
then also shows when the seal existed.
.Pp
The seal and the manifest must read
.Pq as Xr noqtis-inspect 1 reads them
before any TSA is asked.
The request is the SHA-256 of the seal's signature, a random nonce and a
request for the TSA's certificate, sent by an HTTP/1.1 POST; the reply is
stored only once it checks: granted, its imprint the hash of this
signature, its nonce the one sent, and its signature valid under the TSA
certificate at genTime.
Give
.Fl -tsa
more than once for fallbacks: they are tried in order until one gives a
token that checks.
When none does, nothing is written and the exit status is 2.
.Pp
A seal holds one timestamp.
A capsule that already has one is refused unless
.Fl -force
is given, since replacing a timestamp gives up the earlier time it
proves.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -tsa Ar url
A time-stamping authority,
.Ql http://
only: the token is signed by the TSA, so TLS adds no integrity.
At most 32.
.It Fl -anchor Ar der-file
The TSA's root or issuing certificate, DER-encoded: the token must then
also verify under one of the anchors before it is stored.
At most 32.
.It Fl -force
Replace a timestamp the seal already has.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
a timestamp was stored
.It 2
a usage error, a folder that is not a sealed capsule, a timestamp already
there without
.Fl -force ,
or no TSA gave a token that checks (nothing written)
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis seal -k me results
$ noqtis timestamp --tsa http://timestamp.digicert.com results
timestamp from http://timestamp.digicert.com: genTime 2026-10-29T16:02:11Z
timestamped results
$ noqtis check -p me.pub --anchor digicert.der results
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-inspect 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 ,
.Xr nqtsput 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%R RFC 3161
.%T Internet X.509 Public Key Infrastructure Time-Stamp Protocol (TSP)
.Re
